\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Summary of the sample types used in this work. Each row specifies the parent catalogue and construction procedure, the role within the calibration pipeline, and the expected implementation in a real LSST analysis. Samples labelled ``Replaced by'' would be substituted with observational data; ``Simulated by construction'' indicates that augmentation necessarily relies on simulated catalogues even in an operational setting (Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref {sec:3.1}); ``Validation only'' denotes samples retained solely for controlled diagnostic tests.\relax }}{7}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
